# Pairs with RAllOrNothing. A failed dial to the cross-tree barrier drops the
# receiver registry's delegation row, as a catch that "cleans up" an
# unreachable coordinator would. ResolveReceiverDelegatedAsync's catch keeps
# the row and answers Indeterminate; dropping it leaves the txid unknown, so the
# registry answers InFlight and the gate serves the tree's key pre-saga while a
# finalised sibling tree serves its key post-saga.
MODULE: RAllOrNothingDialFailureDropsDelegation
TARGET: RAllOrNothing
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a failed dial to the receiver barrier drops the delegation row, so the tree reads InFlight
PERTURBS: DialFault

--- FIND
    /\ rdial' = [rdial EXCEPT ![tr] = ~rdial[tr]]
    /\ UNCHANGED <<originVars, xtree, netVars, leafVars, rarr, rexp, rdec, rout, rstage, rdeleg, barrierVars, lossVars>>
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the failed dial forgets the delegation.
    /\ rdial' = [rdial EXCEPT ![tr] = ~rdial[tr]]
    /\ rdeleg' = [rdeleg EXCEPT ![tr] = FALSE]
    /\ UNCHANGED <<originVars, xtree, netVars, leafVars, rarr, rexp, rdec, rout, rstage, barrierVars, lossVars>>
--- END
